WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:02.910
I've gotten feedback
that all the Chuck Norris

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.326
imagery in the last video might
have been a little bit too

00:00:05.326 --> 00:00:06.140
overwhelming.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.640
So for this video, I've included
something a little bit more

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.000
soothing.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.140
Let's try to simplify
some more expressions.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.860
And we'll see we're
just applying ideas

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.730
that we already knew about.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:21.250
Let's say I want to simplify the
expression 2 times 3x plus 5.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.020
Well, this literally
means two 3x plus 5's.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.930
So this is the exact same thing.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.750
This is one 3x plus
5, and then to that,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.610
I'm going to add
another 3x plus 5.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.960
This is literally what
2 times 3x plus 5 means.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.330
Well, this is the same thing
as, if we just look at it right

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:40.160
over here, we have now two 3x's.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.000
So we could write
it as 2 times 3x.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:52.490
Plus, we have two 5's,
so plus 2 times 5.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.360
You might say, hey, Sal, isn't
this just the distributive

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.220
property that I know
from arithmetic?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.255
I've essentially just
distributed the 2?

00:00:59.255 --> 00:01:05.690
2 times 3x plus 2 times 5?

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.102
And I would tell
you, yes, it is.

00:01:08.102 --> 00:01:10.560
And the whole reason why I'm
doing this is just to show you

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.250
that it is exactly
what you already know.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.320
But with that out of the way,
let's continue to simplify it.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.430
When you multiply the 2
times the 3x, you get 6x.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:25.030
When you multiply the 2
times the 5, you get 10.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.364
So this simplified
to 6x plus 10.

00:01:28.364 --> 00:01:30.780
Now let's try something that's
a little bit more involved.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.710
Once again, really just
things that you already know.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:54.720
Let's say I had 7 times 3y minus
5 minus 2 times 10 plus 4y.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.410
Let's see if we
can simplify this.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.030
Well, let's work on
the left-hand side

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:02.080
of the expression, the
7 times 3y minus 5.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.560
We just have to
distribute the 7.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.740
This is going to be 7 times 3y,
which is going to give us 21y.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.800
Or if I had 3 y's
7 times, that's

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.770
going to be 21 y's, either way
you want to think about it.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.300
And then I have 7
times-- we've got

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.100
to be careful with
the sign-- negative 5.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.640
7 times negative
5 is negative 35.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.180
So we've simplified
this part of it.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.610
Let's simplify the
right-hand side.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.690
You might be tempted to say,
oh, 2 times 10 and 2 times 4y

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:30.990
and then subtract them.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:34.080
And if you do that right and
you distribute the subtraction,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.190
it would work out.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.357
But I like think of
this as negative 2,

00:02:39.357 --> 00:02:41.190
and we're going to
distribute the negative 2

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:47.790
times 10 and the
negative 2 times 4y.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:53.870
So negative 2 times
10 is negative 20,

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.660
so it's minus 20
right over here.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.130
And then negative 2 times
4, negative 2 times 4

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.860
is negative 8, so it's
going to be negative 8y.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.760
Let's write a minus
8y right over here.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.586
And are we done simplifying?

00:03:08.586 --> 00:03:10.710
Well, no, there's a little
bit more that we can do.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:14.160
We can't add the 21y to the
negative 35 or the negative 20

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.420
because these are
adding different things

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.970
or subtracting different things.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.660
But we do have two things
that are multiplying y.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.620
Let me do all in
this green color.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.720
You have 21 y's right over here.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:33.730
And then we can view it as from
that we are subtracting 8 y's.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.540
So if I have 21 of something
and I take 8 of them away,

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.270
I'm left with 13
of that something.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.190
So those are going to
simplify to 13 y's.

00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:48.310
I'll do this in a new color.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.270
And then I have
negative 35 minus 20.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:56.597
That's just going to
simplify to negative 55.

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:58.680
So this whole thing
simplified, using a little bit

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.810
of the distributive
property and combining

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:06.072
similar or like terms,
we got to 13y minus 55.

